# EvaRoute staff portal (clients/admin) — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust if needed. All values are optional.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL
#   Base URL of the EvaRoute API.
#
#   Leave it EMPTY (the default) to talk to the API through the Vite dev proxy
#   configured in vite.config.js, which forwards /api to http://localhost:3000.
#   Requests are then same-origin: no CORS, and the httpOnly refresh cookie
#   works, so sessions survive past the 15-minute access token.
#
#   Setting an absolute URL (e.g. http://localhost:3000) makes the app call the
#   API cross-origin. That works for Bearer-token requests, but the refresh
#   cookie is dropped: the API answers CORS with
#   "Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *" together with
#   "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true", which browsers reject for
#   credentialed requests. Users then have to sign in again every 15 minutes.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Only used by vite.config.js to pick the dev-proxy target.
# Set it in the shell (not here) if your backend runs on another port:
#   EVAROUTE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:4000 npm run dev
